# Added R21. The refs/ hold (REFS-LICENCE-REVIEW.md, review #15) is a
# redistribution question and only arises on commit. Until each row of
# REFS-MANIFEST.md is individually checked, no reference file or page image is
# committed. Hashes travel in REFS-MANIFEST.md instead; the bytes stay in the
# off-repo backup.
#
# Patterns exclude directory CONTENTS, not the directories, so the negation
# below can re-include session-produced scripts.
**/refs/*
**/pages/*
!**/refs/*.py
!**/pages/*.py

# Build tree: ~124k files. Also excluded from the backup by make_backup.py.
**/.lake/
**/__pycache__/

# Added CT-S21 (M6). The R21 patterns above cover refs/ and pages/ ONLY, and the
# claim that they left zero third-party bytes stageable (R1-107) was FALSE: page
# images and saved pages also live in coldpackets/, in session roots, and in
# outputs/. Nine third-party files were still stageable - two vdPS page images,
# three Jimbo page images, four saved NIST DLMF pages.
#
# Default-deny on media, because the licence question is per file and unresolved:
# the arXiv PDF, for one, is under nonexclusive-distrib/1.0, which grants third
# parties no redistribution right at all. Un-exclude individual files only after
# that file's row in REFS-MANIFEST.md has been checked.
#
# NOTE: this also excludes the operator OWN CC-BY-4.0 companion page images and
# CT-S1-THEOREM/theorem.pdf. That is deliberate - default-deny, then re-admit by
# name - not a judgement that they cannot be committed.
**/*.png
**/*.jpg
**/*.jpeg
**/*.pdf
**/*.html
